# webgl-virgl.flakes: the subtests of WebGL pages that judge.py webgl does
# not judge in the virgl cases, `PATH ERE` a line, PATH as the suite's list
# gives it and ERE an extended regular expression searched for in the
# subtest's message.
#
# occlusion-query-scissor.html: an ANY_SAMPLES_PASSED query whose draws a
# 0x0 scissor rectangle leaves empty reads 1 in 53 to 64 of the page's 65
# such passes, which ones changing from run to run, in both browsers in the
# Debian guest as on Rach2 (dev-log/84-locks/upstream.md); the page's 454
# other subtests passed in every run and are judged.
conformance2/query/occlusion-query-scissor.html ^pass [0-9]+, result: 1 === expected: 0$

# deqp/functional/gles3/texturefiltering/: each of these pages fails every
# one of its 6 or 18 cases with "Image verification failed" in every run, in
# the Debian guest as on Rach2, and the count of the checks that pass inside
# those failed comparisons changes from run to run, by 8 to 920 in three
# runs of the chunk, two in the Debian guest and one on Rach2
# (dev-log/84-locks/upstream.md). The judge would otherwise compare that
# count with one run's.
deqp/functional/gles3/texturefiltering/2d_sizes_02.html : Image verification failed$
